Backport of lxc/incus@a0156d57c1b91af5edf0547ffadd0f1a80bb29b7 (stable-7.0; on main as
52a48d5f2) to v7.0.2 for the isx appliance (Sanne/incus-spawn#2739), unchanged: part of the fix
for GHSA-v855-hxm9-5pwg. The template output limit only truncated the output, and rendering went
on past it. Remove this file once INCUS_VERSION is a release that contains the commit (the next
7.0 release; 7.0.3 is not out yet).

From a0156d57c1b91af5edf0547ffadd0f1a80bb29b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:02:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] incusd/util: Stop the rendering of a template past the output
 limit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The renderer ignores write errors, so the limit only truncated the
output.

This addresses GHSA-v855-hxm9-5pwg (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
(cherry picked from commit a0156d57c1b91af5edf0547ffadd0f1a80bb29b7)
---
 internal/util/template.go | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/internal/util/template.go b/internal/util/template.go
index f621d1551..a049abd68 100644
--- a/internal/util/template.go
+++ b/internal/util/template.go
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ func newTemplateSet() (*pongo2.TemplateSet, error) {
 	return custom, nil
 }
 
-// boundedWriter fails once more than templateMaxOutput bytes have been written.
+// boundedWriter stops the rendering once more than templateMaxOutput bytes have been written.
 type boundedWriter struct {
 	w io.Writer
 	n int
@@ -48,7 +48,8 @@ type boundedWriter struct {
 func (b *boundedWriter) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {
 	b.n += len(p)
 	if b.n > templateMaxOutput {
-		return 0, errors.New("Template output is too large")
+		// The renderer ignores write errors, executeTemplate recovers this.
+		panic("Template output is too large")
 	}
 
 	return b.w.Write(p)
